  "facts": {
    "README.md": "# Orbyss.Foundation.Json\n\nTyped System.Text.Json operations with immutable named profiles. No ASP.NET or CShells dependency.\n\n```csharp\nvar profile = new JsonProfile(new JsonProfileSettings());\nvar request = profile.Deserialize<MyRequest>(utf8);\nvar bytes = profile.Serialize(request);\nvar streamed = await profile.ReadAsync<MyRequest>(stream, cancellationToken);\n```\n\nUse records with required constructor parameters or required properties. Explicitly nullable required\nmembers distinguish missing from null. Strict requests are camel-case, case-sensitive, reject unknown\nand duplicate decoded members, reject numeric strings, honor nullable annotations and required\nconstructors, and default to 1 MiB / depth 32. Limits may be lowered or raised up to 16 MiB / depth 64.\nThe tolerant-response preset permits unknown members and case-insensitive matching, but still rejects\nduplicate logical names, coercion, and malformed Unicode. A null root is rejected.\n\n.NET nullable annotations do not validate collection-element nullability or arbitrary product invariants.\nExpress element requirements with a code-owned converter/validator; this library does not pretend those\nannotations provide a complete schema. Discriminated variants use System.Text.Json polymorphism metadata.\nRegistered converters are trusted code and must preserve their declared contract and remain stateless.\n\nRegister IJsonProfileExtension instances by code, then select their IDs through settings. Unknown,\nduplicate IDs and multiple selected resolvers fail composition. Converter overlap fails when root or\nnested metadata is resolved; resolve known TypeInfo<T>() contracts during activation for early checks.\nNo configuration value is treated as a CLR type. Explicit metadata must come from profile.TypeInfo<T>();\ninstall a source-generated context as an extension Resolver to get the same frozen options. A profile\ndoes not fall back to reflection when a selected resolver lacks a contract.\n\nJsonProfileException exposes deterministic safe codes. Contract/syntax diagnostics omit payloads.\nStream reads enforce the actual byte count regardless of declared content length and honor cancellation.\nServer output uses `JsonResponseContractException` (including `JsonOutputLimitException`), distinct\nfrom client `JsonProfileException`. Native serialization admits retained bytes through a bounded\nbuffer before returning output. Each ordinary string and dictionary key is counted with the native\nencoder before encoding, including near-cap scalar failures. Retained bytes never exceed MaxBytes;\nnative contiguous scratch reservations are finite at `6 * MaxBytes + 4096`, and oversized reservations\nfail before allocation. This is an explicit scratch bound, not a claim that heap use equals wire size.\nCancellation is observed before serialization and at buffer operations. Consumers publish only after\nsuccessful admission and keep object construction bounded too.\n\nString conversion is reserved for bounded native encoding; overlapping string converters fail metadata\nadmission. Trusted converters must remain bounded and delegate string values through\n`JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, value, options)` to retain scalar admission. Converter-internal\nallocation/semantic ownership still requires ordinary source review.\n\n`JsonProfileKeys`, `JsonProfileKey` and `JsonProfileRequirement` describe explicit selection and\nsupported preset/capacity/depth intervals. Runtime values live in configured settings. `ValueSequenceJsonExtension`\nadapts `Collections.Core.ValueSequence<T>` to arrays; it also works with generated closed contract\nmetadata. The Core collection owns shallow snapshots and ordered equality without serializer dependencies.\n\n`CanonicalUtf8Writer` supplies strict UTF-8, minimal JSON escaping, finite byte admission and incremental\nSHA-256 with fixed scratch space. It preserves caller-specified order and does not normalize or sort.\nA null destination hashes/counts without an aggregate byte array. Callers own destination disposal and\npublish only after `CompleteSha256`; overflow, malformed Unicode and destination failure prevent sealing.\n\n## Canonicalization and compatibility\n\nJsonCanonicalizer.Canonicalize accepts the explicit algorithm\n`rfc8785-reject-negative-zero-v1`: UTF-16 ordinal object keys, unchanged arrays, exact strings without\nUnicode normalization, finite binary64 number interpretation and ECMAScript decimal placement, UTF-8\nbytes. Negative zero is rejected under RFC erratum 7920. Do not use it for arbitrary-precision identities.\n\nRawJsonNumber preserves a numeric token lexeme through typed serialization. It is a compatibility\nprimitive, not RFC 8785. Product normalization (including answer ordering), authorization and deduplication\nremain product-owned. RM-01 captured numeric `raw`/`normalized` values are strings; preserve them exactly.\nDo not replace legacy readers or wire algorithms without old byte/digest fixtures and version review.\n\nThe dependency assessment and approved implementation exception are in\n[the repository decision record](https://github.com/orbyss-io/dotnet-foundation/blob/main/docs/json-canonicalization-decision.md).\nRun `python tests/validate_json.py` after the Release build; Node provides independent V8 vectors.\n",
    "lib/net10.0/Orbyss.Foundation.Json.xml": "<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<doc>\n    <assembly>\n        <name>Orbyss.Foundation.Json</name>\n    </assembly>\n    <members>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer\">\n            <summary>Separates finite serializer scratch reservations from admitted retained JSON bytes.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.#ctor(System.Int32,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <summary>Separates finite serializer scratch reservations from admitted retained JSON bytes.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.retained\">\n            <summary>Retains only bytes admitted within the output limit.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.scratch\">\n            <summary>Provides a bounded contiguous reservation required by the native JSON writer.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.length\">\n            <summary>Tracks committed output, independent of scratch reservation size.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.ToArray\">\n            <summary>Copies only a successfully sealed admitted result.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.Advance(System.Int32)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.GetMemory(System.Int32)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.GetSpan(System.Int32)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedJsonBuffer.Reserve(System.Int32)\">\n            <summary>Bounds reservations before allocation, including native worst-case UTF-16 JSON escaping.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter\">\n            <summary>Admits each native string/key before Utf8JsonWriter can reserve and encode an oversized scalar.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter.#ctor(System.Int32)\">\n            <summary>Admits each native string/key before Utf8JsonWriter can reserve and encode an oversized scalar.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter.Read(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonReader@,System.Type,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter.ReadAsPropertyName(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonReader@,System.Type,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter.Write(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonWriter,System.String,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter.WriteAsPropertyName(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonWriter,System.String,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.BoundedStringJsonConverter.Admit(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonWriter,System.String,System.Text.Encodings.Web.JavaScriptEncoder,System.Int32)\">\n            <summary>Counts native encoded scalar bytes with fixed scratch storage before retaining its output.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer\">\n            <summary>Writes caller-owned schema order with minimal JSON escaping and incremental SHA-256.</summary>\n            <remarks>Does not normalize/sort or implement RFC 8785. The caller owns the destination and publishes only after completion.</remarks>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.Utf8\">\n            <summary>Rejects malformed Unicode instead of replacing its bytes.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.destination\">\n            <summary>References caller-owned output, or no output in hashing mode.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.maximumBytes\">\n            <summary>Caps total admitted representation bytes.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.hash\">\n            <summary>Owns only native incremental digest state.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.completed\">\n            <summary>Prevents writing or resealing after success.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.failed\">\n            <summary>Prevents publishing a digest after a partial failed write.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.disposed\">\n            <summary>Tracks disposal of owned digest state.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.ByteCount\">\n            <summary>Gets the admitted encoded byte count.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.#ctor(System.Int64,System.IO.Stream)\">\n            <summary>Creates a bounded writer. A null destination hashes/counts without retaining aggregate output.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.Raw(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Char})\">\n            <summary>Encodes an owned syntax fragment using strict Unicode and fixed-size scratch space.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.RawUtf8(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})\">\n            <summary>Copies validated UTF-8 without decoding or retaining another aggregate buffer.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.String(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Encodes literal Unicode, short control escapes and lowercase remaining control escapes; null stays null.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.CompleteSha256\">\n            <summary>Seals the successful byte stream and returns its lowercase SHA-256. Further writes fail.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.Dispose\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.RequireActive\">\n            <summary>Rejects operations after success, failure or disposal.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.Admit(System.Int32)\">\n            <summary>Rejects overflow before retaining additional output.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.CanonicalUtf8Writer.Append(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})\">\n            <summary>Writes admitted bytes and hashes exactly the same order.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.GuardedJsonTypeInfoResolver\">\n            <summary>Rejects converter overlap for root and nested types before metadata is used.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.GuardedJsonTypeInfoResolver.#ctor(System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.IJsonTypeInfoResolver)\">\n            <summary>Rejects converter overlap for root and nested types before metadata is used.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.GuardedJsonTypeInfoResolver.GetTypeInfo(System.Type,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.IJsonProfileExtension\">\n            <summary>Supplies stateless code-owned converters or a metadata resolver under an allowlisted identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.IJsonProfileExtension.Id\">\n            <summary>Gets the unique configuration identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.IJsonProfileExtension.Converters\">\n            <summary>Gets converters to install. Overlap is rejected for each resolved type.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.IJsonProfileExtension.Resolver\">\n            <summary>Gets optional source-generated or custom metadata. Select at most one resolver per profile.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonCanonicalizer\">\n            <summary>Implements bounded RFC 8785 canonical UTF-8 with explicit negative-zero rejection.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonCanonicalizer.Algorithm\">\n            <summary>Identifies RFC 8785 with verified erratum 7920 negative-zero rejection.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonCanonicalizer.Canonicalize(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.String,System.Int32,System.Int32)\">\n            <summary>Canonicalizes one value without product normalization or array reordering.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonCanonicalizer.AppendValue(System.Text.StringBuilder,System.Text.Json.JsonElement)\">\n            <summary>Writes ordered objects, unchanged arrays, exact strings, and binary64 numbers.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonCanonicalizer.AppendString(System.Text.StringBuilder,System.String)\">\n            <summary>Writes RFC 8785 string escapes without HTML or Unicode normalization.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonCanonicalizer.FormatNumber(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Applies ECMAScript decimal/exponent placement to .NET's shortest round-trip binary64 digits.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes\">\n            <summary>Names stable JSON admission and output failure classifications owned by Foundation.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.SizeExceeded\">\n            <summary>Client JSON exceeds its decoded byte budget.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.DuplicateMember\">\n            <summary>Client JSON contains a duplicate decoded member name.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.InvalidContract\">\n            <summary>Client JSON violates its declared typed contract.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.InvalidSyntax\">\n            <summary>Client JSON contains invalid syntax.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.InvalidUnicode\">\n            <summary>Client JSON contains invalid Unicode.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.NullRoot\">\n            <summary>Client JSON has an inadmissible null root.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.NegativeZero\">\n            <summary>The selected canonical algorithm rejects negative zero.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.NumberNotRepresentable\">\n            <summary>The selected canonical algorithm cannot represent a number.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.ResponseSizeExceeded\">\n            <summary>Server JSON exceeds its output byte budget.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.ResponseInvalidContract\">\n            <summary>Server JSON violates its declared typed contract.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.ResponseInvalidUnicode\">\n            <summary>Server JSON contains invalid Unicode.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.ResponseNullRoot\">\n            <summary>Server JSON has an inadmissible null root.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.RequestProfileBypass\">\n            <summary>An operation bypasses its declared request reader.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.ResponseProfileBypass\">\n            <summary>An operation bypasses its declared response factory.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonFailureCodes.PageSizeInvalid\">\n            <summary>The requested page count exceeds configured admission.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonOutputLimitException\">\n            <summary>Reports server output exceeding its declared capacity. It is not a client request failure.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonOutputLimitException.#ctor\">\n            <summary>Creates a safe capacity failure without retaining private payload data.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile\">\n            <summary>Provides typed, bounded JSON operations over frozen serializer options.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.options\">\n            <summary>Stores immutable serializer options.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.MaxBytes\">\n            <summary>Gets the maximum encoded size.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.MaxDepth\">\n            <summary>Gets the maximum nesting depth.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.Preset\">\n            <summary>Gets the admitted parser/serializer preset identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings,System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable{Orbyss.Foundation.Json.IJsonProfileExtension})\">\n            <summary>Compiles a fixed preset and explicitly selected stateless extensions.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.TypeInfo``1\">\n            <summary>Resolves metadata governed by this profile; source-generated resolvers receive the same options.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.Deserialize``1(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})\">\n            <summary>Deserializes a known contract with this profile's metadata.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.Deserialize``1(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte},System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfo{``0})\">\n            <summary>Deserializes with explicit metadata belonging to this immutable profile.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.Serialize``1(``0)\">\n            <summary>Serializes a known contract, retaining explicitly nullable members.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.Serialize``1(``0,System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfo{``0})\">\n            <summary>Serializes with explicit profile-governed metadata.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.Serialize``1(``0,System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfo{``0},System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <summary>Serializes within finite retained/scratch bounds and observes caller cancellation before commitment.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.ReadAsync``1(System.IO.Stream,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <summary>Reads at most the configured byte limit plus one detection byte, honoring cancellation.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.ValidateInput(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})\">\n            <summary>Rejects malformed Unicode, duplicate decoded keys, excessive depth, and extra roots before typed conversion.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile.RequireOptions(System.Text.Json.Serialization.Metadata.JsonTypeInfo)\">\n            <summary>Prevents supplied metadata from bypassing the selected profile's guarantees.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileCatalog\">\n            <summary>Holds an immutable named catalog scoped to its owning application or shell.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileCatalog.profiles\">\n            <summary>Stores the compiled profiles.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileCatalog.#ctor(System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary{System.String,Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings},System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable{Orbyss.Foundation.Json.IJsonProfileExtension})\">\n            <summary>Compiles all profiles and allowlisted registrations.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileCatalog.Get(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Gets a deliberately selected named profile or fails closed.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileCatalog.Get(Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKey)\">\n            <summary>Resolves an explicitly selected typed profile key.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileException\">\n            <summary>Reports a deterministic JSON admission failure without carrying authored payloads.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileException.#ctor(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Creates a classified admission failure.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileException.Code\">\n            <summary>Gets the stable application-independent error code.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKey\">\n            <summary>Identifies a deliberately selected configured profile rather than implicit global options.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKey.Name\">\n            <summary>Gets the configuration key.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKey.#ctor(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Admits a bounded key without changing its identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKeys\">\n            <summary>Exports preserved preset identities and standard configured profile keys.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKeys.StrictRequest\">\n            <summary>Strict request admission preset/key.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKeys.TolerantResponse\">\n            <summary>Tolerant response reading preset/key.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKeys.SuccessResponse\">\n            <summary>Standard bounded success/page profile key.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileKeys.ProblemResponse\">\n            <summary>Standard bounded problem profile key.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement\">\n            <summary>Declares supported contract capacity/strictness; deployment budgets stay in profile settings.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.#ctor(System.String,System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Int32)\">\n            <summary>Creates a supported interval and strictness requirement.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.Preset\">\n            <summary>Gets required strictness.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.MinimumBytes\">\n            <summary>Gets minimum supported capacity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.MaximumBytes\">\n            <summary>Gets maximum supported capacity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.MinimumDepth\">\n            <summary>Gets minimum supported nesting depth.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.MaximumDepth\">\n            <summary>Gets maximum supported nesting depth.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileRequirement.Validate(Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfile)\">\n            <summary>Rejects a configured profile outside supported guarantees.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings\">\n            <summary>Configures a named profile using fixed admission presets and allowlisted code extensions.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings.Preset\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets strict-request or tolerant-response.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings.MaxBytes\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the maximum input/output size, capped at 16 MiB.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings.MaxDepth\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the maximum nesting depth, capped at 64.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonProfileSettings.Extensions\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets code-registered extension identities.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonResponseContractException\">\n            <summary>Reports a server output contract failure without exposing its payload or serializer details.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonResponseContractException.Code\">\n            <summary>Gets the stable server failure classification.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.JsonResponseContractException.#ctor(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Creates a safe output failure classification.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumber\">\n            <summary>Retains a validated numeric token exactly for product-owned legacy wire contracts.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumber.#ctor(System.String)\">\n            <summary>Validates one complete numeric token without normalizing it.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumber.Text\">\n            <summary>Gets exact token text. A default value is invalid for serialization.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumberConverter\">\n            <summary>Preserves number lexemes without routine application property walking.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumberConverter.Read(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonReader@,System.Type,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumberConverter.Write(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonWriter,Orbyss.Foundation.Json.RawJsonNumber,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverter`1\">\n            <summary>Typed array converter usable directly with generated contract metadata.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverter`1.HandleNull\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverter`1.Read(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonReader@,System.Type,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverter`1.Write(System.Text.Json.Utf8JsonWriter,Orbyss.Foundation.Collections.Core.ValueSequence{`0},System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverterFactory\">\n            <summary>Creates array adapters only for the owned collection type.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverterFactory.CanConvert(System.Type)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonConverterFactory.CreateConverter(System.Type,System.Text.Json.JsonSerializerOptions)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonExtension\">\n            <summary>Allowlisted JSON array adaptation for owned collection values.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonExtension.ExtensionId\">\n            <summary>Names this code-owned extension for profile configuration.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonExtension.Id\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonExtension.Converters\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.Json.ValueSequenceJsonExtension.Resolver\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n    </members>\n</doc>\n",
    "orbyss-foundation/settings.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"packageId\": \"Orbyss.Foundation.Json\",\n  \"packageVersion\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"sourceSha256\": {\n    \"BoundedJsonBuffer.cs\": \"42a8fed226c1f9e150e8210a07227fdc246c4f0e949db227757e8150105be8aa\",\n    \"BoundedStringJsonConverter.cs\": \"9a3e74c190bf8123254171f94cf825c24834c37ef15ca1496414113e523e290c\",\n    \"CanonicalUtf8Writer.cs\": \"399e1ff38f0c416357ca8e2e1574abe6a187cd1327b8b901ee04ef0b439299c8\",\n    \"GuardedJsonTypeInfoResolver.cs\": \"796fc5264ed316555091a38e9d0014ff911122984a01c4b80e2bff0455b510e9\",\n    \"IJsonProfileExtension.cs\": \"1e588bb6dd552d500e727c52ee13d3522651a665c67e94c9386b35081affb423\",\n    \"JsonCanonicalizer.cs\": \"bfad6ba1bcc0d709367a2388c7734f8faa0ce0d14ad4a48e7a07b998e1a022fc\",\n    \"JsonFailureCodes.cs\": \"35918142a1742b91f794293db825cc3c9ec22cbbe57bf73f864ed212b3dad6dd\",\n    \"JsonOutputLimitException.cs\": \"d0d56badf47b3d3fd657cef25c093b335d69d1688ee5f5ea2a76cb1b0e9d70ad\",\n    \"JsonProfile.cs\": \"22d96ae37b673ed4a2693dbf4621d5cae73e36d3acdc97875a720ac2f1688b1b\",\n    \"JsonProfileCatalog.cs\": \"8c7a8689284472637b180139215fbaa4e1bec12aff27c9318ae3c97a7a3bc544\",\n    \"JsonProfileException.cs\": \"e4a010341d94cfe12777baa0a664f246c46009381ce782f5808ba5b337f73258\",\n    \"JsonProfileKey.cs\": \"4314e0bb610a9a1ab895b6214d868741c626e4a690e3fc601aa7064047cffb39\",\n    \"JsonProfileKeys.cs\": \"88b78861a4f6a6b6f741810b92d0a28ea4f53a293cf567ad9aa31c46d39ee6ff\",\n    \"JsonProfileRequirement.cs\": \"22b1a6881e437c6923038bbc5b30827493e9b7486dd79180f809abcaf9b395ea\",\n    \"JsonProfileSettings.cs\": \"afdce8c5489ccc86cfb8fd5845fb7fca1210986cf0c453b9e72f48ed72769d21\",\n    \"JsonResponseContractException.cs\": \"4359c334f78f42c9d776c3bda9f4eed51b42508a84b56b38931d12c486ce4510\",\n    \"RawJsonNumber.cs\": \"ac04414581bb6ad01d3df7dd57947210a39cbbbafef1f26b65701231275ba2ca\",\n    \"RawJsonNumberConverter.cs\": \"b415dd752f25c840f37c74214ffebd26894e