{
  "id": "Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql",
  "version": "0.3.1",
  "license": "MIT",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/orbyss-io/dotnet-foundation",
    "commit": "aa7ae11678b0dbcf96af009e347d06673a9dce06"
  },
  "payloadFiles": {
    "_rels/.rels": "e2a3db704c3a74514fe0daa7213fe8fe0dda312619d7656cfecc99d17ef0f54a",
    "Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.nuspec": "5cd432b8a7f5611f46be245d8fe8a8ad37f52a2eab6743fd081c66daf6b13972",
    "README.md": "609cf973a790e357d662cc14d8656d2bb5354391497acf7f5281ade6acfe725c",
    "lib/net10.0/Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.dll": "fb408e32bd05bad3477c7425157bd050bb905994070ed1b796d50f251eda0f7d",
    "lib/net10.0/Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.xml": "da7e7716620439e180b1cf796e400b61c0419289b6fc632b668600b2b78d5daf",
    "orbyss-foundation/settings.json": "207b81086f38d3e4be93a14c72fd748c7e274993668eada8f2b7ab062491a69d",
    "[Content_Types].xml": "603043d59dee554187eacd0a3dee5070b5b1b540a33b1f079da81f1a28a8fe69",
    "package/services/metadata/core-properties/nuget.psmdcp": "8e25231a1a35c713f3c19e7af87e7d70fa886497f7b8298ca179961012229e61"
  },
  "facts": {
    "README.md": "# Orbyss Foundation PostgreSQL\n\nThe consumer's persistence feature registers its native context with `AddFoundationPostgreSql<TContext>`.\nTyped policies bind from `Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:<name>` or are supplied explicitly. A stable\nkeyed `NpgsqlDataSource` belongs to each shell provider generation and policy. Context pooling is not used.\nConnection, command, lock and cancellation acknowledgement settings are validated once; operation stage\ncaps do not rewrite connection strings or create additional pool identities.\n\nContexts derive from `FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext` in their persistence project. Its sealed native\ndisposal methods release factory reservations only after EF disposal completes, including concurrent\nand repeated disposal. EF has no context-disposal interceptor, so this intentional native base establishes\nthe lifetime guarantee without reflecting internal state or trusting an extra caller callback.\nThe context constructor must pass the admitted options to its base unchanged. Provider selection is\nsealed in `OnConfiguring`; application entities and mappings remain in the context's `OnModelCreating`.\n\nResolve `IPostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory<TContext>` and `await using` its unit, then independently `await using`\neach context created through `unit.Factory.CreateDbContextAsync`. Units begin actual `IShell.BeginScope`\non the exact owning generation; ordinary root/plain-DI factory creation is rejected. Initialization,\nbackground work and evaluation cleanup use the same path. Closing a unit stops admission but retains its\ntracked scope until existing contexts dispose. Datasource teardown also waits for its context holds.\nConcurrent and repeated owner disposal observe the same owner-close outcome, including delayed or\nfailed final scope disposal. An early close with live contexts stops admission immediately; those\ncontexts own final scope release and any failure from that release.\n\nUse the deadline token for database calls and pass an existing outer deadline to follow-up/reconciliation\nunits. Caller cancellation does not establish rollback or commit certainty. The package owns no schema,\nentities, transaction contents, retry policy or domain outcome mapping. `PostgreSqlFailureInfo` exposes\nonly SQLSTATE and constraint identity for consumer-owned classification; it excludes provider messages and SQL.\nPass `unit.Deadline.Token` explicitly to `BeginTransactionAsync`, `CommitAsync` and `RollbackAsync`.\nNative transaction dispatch has no automatic command-stage cap; a consumer may own a narrower stage\nwhen its policy requires one. Async EF command dispatch receives the capped stage token, and sync\ncompletion checks elapsed time. A canceled sync command may already have committed; reconcile its\nreceipt through a fresh unit instead of inferring rollback. Native reader-close events release command\nstages after drain/cleanup even when EF's later disposal notification is skipped by a close fault.\n\nProvider-owned EF and Npgsql logging preserves native categories, event IDs and severity plus safe\nexception type/SQLSTATE classifications. It discards native SQL/parameter state, raw exception text and\nnative scope payloads, and explicitly disables parameter logging on each stable datasource. Application\nambient correlation remains available through the destination logging factory. The package does not\nchange process-global logging configuration or take ownership of the application's logger factory.\n\nThe native qualifier uses an owned ephemeral PostgreSQL container with no retained volume. Its explicit\n`--deadline-only` mode exercises deterministic deadlines without Docker and does not claim database acceptance.\n",
    "lib/net10.0/Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.xml": "<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<doc>\n    <assembly>\n        <name>Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql</name>\n    </assembly>\n    <members>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1\">\n            <summary>Attaches a scoped factory to an explicitly owned tracked shell lease.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.gate\">\n            <summary>Serializes owner closure and context reservations.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.scope\">\n            <summary>The actual CShells tracked scope, retained until the last context leaves.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.references\">\n            <summary>The number of owner/context references retaining that scope.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.closed\">\n            <summary>Rejects new units after the owner closes admission.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.ownerClosure\">\n            <summary>Retains the owner's one pending/completed/faulted close outcome for all disposal callers.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.Deadline\">\n            <summary>The owned deadline spanning this lease's independent contexts.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.DataSource\">\n            <summary>The selected generation's datasource.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.Policy\">\n            <summary>The immutable native policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.Initialize(CShells.Lifecycle.IShellScope,Orbyss.Foundation.Execution.Core.IExecutionDeadline,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy)\">\n            <summary>Enables a factory only from the tracked lease adapter.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.Acquire\">\n            <summary>Rejects root/plain-DI/out-of-lease creation and reserves both source and tracked scope.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.CloseAsync\">\n            <summary>Closes new admission while retaining the scope for contexts already in use.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.CompleteOwnerClosureAsync(System.Threading.Tasks.TaskCompletionSource)\">\n            <summary>Publishes closure before disposal callbacks can reenter the owner.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.ReleaseAsync\">\n            <summary>Disposes the tracked scope exactly after its final reference is released.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState`1.DisposeOwnedScopeAsync(CShells.Lifecycle.IShellScope)\">\n            <summary>Releases timers and tracked ownership after all contexts have finished.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext\">\n            <summary>Native EF context base that ties disposal to its factory-owned shell/data-source hold.</summary>\n            <remarks>Use only in the persistence implementation. It owns no application entities or transaction policy.</remarks>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.#ctor(Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptions)\">\n            <summary>Native EF context base that ties disposal to its factory-owned shell/data-source hold.</summary>\n            <remarks>Use only in the persistence implementation. It owns no application entities or transaction policy.</remarks>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.creationOptions\">\n            <summary>The exact native options admitted by the selected registration adapter.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.lease\">\n            <summary>The context's admitted tracked reservation.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.disposal\">\n            <summary>Publishes one disposal task for sync/async/concurrent callers.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.Deadline\">\n            <summary>Gets the operation deadline; use its token for application-owned database calls.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.DataSourceId\">\n            <summary>Gets the non-secret stable source identity for this provider generation/policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.Lease\">\n            <summary>Gets the admitted native policy and tracked hold for interceptors.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.AttachLease(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptions)\">\n            <summary>Attaches the factory hold before the context can perform I/O.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.OnConfiguring(Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptionsBuilder)\">\n            <summary>Native provider selection belongs to registration; contexts retain their own model mapping.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.Dispose\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.DisposeAsync\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.DisposeCoreAsync(System.Threading.Tasks.TaskCompletionSource)\">\n            <summary>Completes native disposal before releasing datasource and tracked scope ownership.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlServiceCollectionExtensions\">\n            <summary>Registers provider-owned policies and context mechanics through the consumer's provider feature.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlServiceCollectionExtensions.AddFoundationPostgreSql``1(Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.IServiceCollection,CShells.ShellSettings,System.String,System.Func{Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptions{``0},``0})\">\n            <summary>Binds one policy from Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies without starting application storage initialization.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.FoundationPostgreSqlServiceCollectionExtensions.AddFoundationPostgreSql``1(Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.IServiceCollection,System.String,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions,System.Func{Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptions{``0},``0})\">\n            <summary>Registers one stable keyed datasource, scoped nonpooled context factory and exact-generation lease adapter.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.IPostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory`1\">\n            <summary>Owns tracked shell scopes for initialization, requests, background work and cleanup alike.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.IPostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory`1.BeginUnitAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken,Orbyss.Foundation.Execution.Core.IExecutionDeadline)\">\n            <summary>Creates an owned scope with a deadline capped by the supplied complete-operation deadline.</summary>\n            <param name=\"callerCancellation\">Cancellation for this operation when no outer deadline is supplied.</param>\n            <param name=\"operationDeadline\">An optional already owned complete-operation deadline; it is never reset.</param>\n            <returns>The lease. Contexts created through it must each be independently disposed.</returns>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory`1\">\n            <summary>Creates independent contexts only in an admitted tracked shell scope.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory`1.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState{`0},Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextRegistration{`0},Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger{Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory{`0}},Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILoggerFactory)\">\n            <summary>Creates independent contexts only in an admitted tracked shell scope.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory`1.CreateDbContext\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory`1.CreateDbContextAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor\">\n            <summary>Owns command stages and retains reader-stage cancellation until disposal.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.#ctor(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger)\">\n            <summary>Owns command stages and retains reader-stage cancellation until disposal.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.stages\">\n            <summary>Holds stages only for commands currently executing.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ReaderExecuting(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult{System.Data.Common.DbDataReader})\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ReaderExecutingAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult{System.Data.Common.DbDataReader},System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ReaderExecuted(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandExecutedEventData,System.Data.Common.DbDataReader)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ReaderExecutedAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandExecutedEventData,System.Data.Common.DbDataReader,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.DataReaderDisposing(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.DataReaderDisposingEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.NonQueryExecuting(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult{System.Int32})\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.NonQueryExecutingAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult{System.Int32},System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.NonQueryExecuted(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandExecutedEventData,System.Int32)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.NonQueryExecutedAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandExecutedEventData,System.Int32,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ScalarExecuting(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult{System.Object})\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ScalarExecutingAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult{System.Object},System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ScalarExecuted(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandExecutedEventData,System.Object)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.ScalarExecutedAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandExecutedEventData,System.Object,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.CommandFailed(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandErrorEventData)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.CommandFailedAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandErrorEventData,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.CommandCanceled(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEndEventData)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.CommandCanceledAsync(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEndEventData,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.Begin(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.CommandEventData,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <summary>Reserves a stage before any native command starts.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.Check(System.Data.Common.DbCommand)\">\n            <summary>Rejects completion after expiry; cancellation never establishes rollback.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.RetainThroughNativeClose(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,System.Data.Common.DbDataReader)\">\n            <summary>Retains cancellation through native drain, including faults before EF's disposing notification.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.End(System.Data.Common.DbCommand)\">\n            <summary>Releases a completed/failed command stage.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage\">\n            <summary>Owns one command cap and best-effort native cancellation through complete reader consumption.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.deadline\">\n            <summary>The independently owned capped command deadline.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.cancellation\">\n            <summary>Owns the driver's cancellation registration.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.disposed\">\n            <summary>Guards repeated reader/command cleanup.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.#ctor(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease,System.Threading.CancellationToken,Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger)\">\n            <summary>Configures a command without changing its datasource/pool identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.Token\">\n            <summary>Gets stage cancellation for native dispatch and retained reader consumption.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.ThrowIfExpired\">\n            <summary>Checks monotonic expiry even if timer callback dispatch is delayed.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.Dispose\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlCommandStage.TryCancel(System.Data.Common.DbCommand,Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger)\">\n            <summary>Requests native cancellation; driver acknowledgement/failure remains visible to the operation.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor\">\n            <summary>Runs native connection/pool admission inside a capped deadline and sets owned lock waits.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.ConnectionOpening(System.Data.Common.DbConnection,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.ConnectionEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.ConnectionOpeningAsync(System.Data.Common.DbConnection,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.ConnectionEventData,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.InterceptionResult,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.ConnectionOpened(System.Data.Common.DbConnection,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.ConnectionEndEventData)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.ConnectionOpenedAsync(System.Data.Common.DbConnection,Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Diagnostics.ConnectionEndEventData,System.Threading.CancellationToken)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.Admit(Orbyss.Foundation.Execution.Core.IExecutionDeadline)\">\n            <summary>Rejects elapsed stages even when timer callbacks or native cancellation dispatch are delayed.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.CloseRejectedConnectionAsync(System.Data.Common.DbConnection,System.Exception)\">\n            <summary>Returns no rejected open/setup connection as healthy; preserves both failures if native cleanup fails.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease\">\n            <summary>Releases one native datasource and tracked scope reservation exactly once.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.Execution.Core.IExecutionDeadline,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy,System.Func{System.Threading.Tasks.ValueTask})\">\n            <summary>Releases one native datasource and tracked scope reservation exactly once.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease.released\">\n            <summary>Guards concurrent/double context disposal.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease.Deadline\">\n            <summary>Gets the outer monotonic deadline.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease.DataSource\">\n            <summary>Gets the stable native source.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease.Policy\">\n            <summary>Gets the immutable stage policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextLease.DisposeAsync\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextRegistration`1\">\n            <summary>Retains one immutable native context registration per shell policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextRegistration`1.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy,System.Func{Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.DbContextOptions{`0},`0})\">\n            <summary>Retains one immutable native context registration per shell policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlFailureInfo\">\n            <summary>Safe native failure identity; messages, SQL, detail, credentials and private input are excluded.</summary>\n            <param name=\"SqlState\">The native five-character SQLSTATE identity.</param>\n            <param name=\"ConstraintName\">The provider's exact optional schema constraint name.</param>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlFailureInfo.#ctor(System.String,System.String)\">\n            <summary>Safe native failure identity; messages, SQL, detail, credentials and private input are excluded.</summary>\n            <param name=\"SqlState\">The native five-character SQLSTATE identity.</param>\n            <param name=\"ConstraintName\">The provider's exact optional schema constraint name.</param>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlFailureInfo.SqlState\">\n            <summary>The native five-character SQLSTATE identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlFailureInfo.ConstraintName\">\n            <summary>The provider's exact optional schema constraint name.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlFailureInfo.TryRead(System.Exception,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlFailureInfo@)\">\n            <summary>Extracts native identity through a bounded exception chain without classifying application outcomes.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions\">\n            <summary>Deployment-owned native database budgets, validated into an immutable provider snapshot.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions.ConnectionString\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the policy's connection string; it is never emitted as a diagnostic.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions.OperationTimeout\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the complete operation budget.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions.ConnectionTimeout\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the capped connection/open/pool wait budget.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions.CommandTimeout\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the cap for each command.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions.LockTimeout\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the native PostgreSQL lock wait cap.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions.CancellationTimeout\">\n            <summary>Gets or sets the driver's cancellation acknowledgement allowance.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy\">\n            <summary>Admits native configuration once, retaining one pool identity for this provider generation/policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.ConnectionString\">\n            <summary>The stable validated connection string owned by the datasource.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.OperationTimeout\">\n            <summary>The operation lifetime shared by its independent context units.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.ConnectionTimeout\">\n            <summary>The maximum native open/pool wait stage.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.CommandTimeout\">\n            <summary>The maximum command stage.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.LockTimeout\">\n            <summary>The native lock timeout.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions)\">\n            <summary>Validates budgets and configures native driver fallbacks once, never per operation.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.Seconds(System.TimeSpan)\">\n            <summary>Projects a positive stage to the driver's whole-second fallback without disabling it.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.Matches(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy)\">\n            <summary>Requires registrations sharing one policy name to select exactly one native configuration.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy.Validate(System.TimeSpan)\">\n            <summary>Rejects disabled and out-of-range native timer values.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLogger\">\n            <summary>Forwards only provider-owned safe fields; ambient application correlation stays in the destination.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLogger.#ctor(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILogger)\">\n            <summary>Forwards only provider-owned safe fields; ambient application correlation stays in the destination.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLogger.BeginScope``1(``0)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLogger.IsEnabled(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.LogLevel)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLogger.Log``1(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.LogLevel,Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.EventId,``0,System.Exception,System.Func{``0,System.Exception,System.String})\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory\">\n            <summary>Preserves native diagnostic classification without forwarding SQL, parameters or raw exceptions.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory.#ctor(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILoggerFactory)\">\n            <summary>Preserves native diagnostic classification without forwarding SQL, parameters or raw exceptions.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory.CreateLogger(System.String)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory.AddProvider(Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILoggerProvider)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory.Dispose\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1\">\n            <summary>An owned tracked shell scope whose active contexts retain its datasource until disposal.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1.state\">\n            <summary>Owns admission and final tracked scope release.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ContextLeaseState{`0},Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.IDbContextFactory{`0})\">\n            <summary>Creates the public owned unit around its scoped native factory.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1.Factory\">\n            <summary>Gets the nonpooled native factory; each invocation creates an independent unit.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1.Deadline\">\n            <summary>Gets the deadline retained by this unit and its contexts.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1.DataSourceId\">\n            <summary>Gets a stable non-secret source identity.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLease`1.DisposeAsync\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory`1\">\n            <summary>Begins tracked scopes on its exact shell generation, including during initialization.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory`1.#ctor(CShells.Lifecycle.IShell,Orbyss.Foundation.Execution.Core.IExecutionDeadlineFactory,Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlContextRegistration{`0})\">\n            <summary>Begins tracked scopes on its exact shell generation, including during initialization.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory`1.BeginUnitAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken,Orbyss.Foundation.Execution.Core.IExecutionDeadline)\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"T:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource\">\n            <summary>Retains one native datasource until all factory-created context holds drain.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.gate\">\n            <summary>Serializes admission, release and disposal.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.drained\">\n            <summary>Signals completion of all active context holds during teardown.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.active\">\n            <summary>The outstanding native context-unit count.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.closing\">\n            <summary>Prevents new context admission after teardown begins.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"F:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.disposal\">\n            <summary>Publishes one shared disposal task for concurrent callers.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.Source\">\n            <summary>Gets the stable native source selected by the policy.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"P:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.Id\">\n            <summary>Gets a non-secret provider-generation identity for qualification/diagnostics.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.#ctor(Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlPolicy,Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.ILoggerFactory)\">\n            <summary>Builds an admitted source; opening connections remains operation-owned.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.Acquire\">\n            <summary>Admits a context hold only while this generation's datasource is available.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.Release\">\n            <summary>Releases a context hold after native context disposal has completed.</summary>\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.DisposeAsync\">\n            <inheritdoc />\n        </member>\n        <member name=\"M:Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.DisposeCoreAsync\">\n            <summary>Waits for units even if host emergency teardown bypasses its ordinary scope wait.</summary>\n        </member>\n    </members>\n</doc>\n",
    "orbyss-foundation/settings.json": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"packageId\": \"Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql\",\n  \"packageVersion\": \"0.3.1\",\n  \"sourceSha256\": {\n    \"ContextLeaseState.cs\": \"0374fda52f16c84224d3b72cb862ef141150f6ffbb38187398cccab1042752c6\",\n    \"FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.cs\": \"f7607fa8ba617c90d28234ba48b897c774ad84fce9be7ae7d4c53260fa8833ab\",\n    \"FoundationPostgreSqlServiceCollectionExtensions.cs\": \"6e8c7c5d76b1b35522542fdeb9db50411e6308062d01f6ed0fb69a9d59f6a02b\",\n    \"IPostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory.cs\": \"6280f1fc36cafe2c3e5f64de049f0f7494a10e4c80e89dbc422f1775ac8c0b3b\",\n    \"OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory.cs\": \"9472b0df3f4b7fe9ae5f586a116f8f22f22d49cdc591cb7283041d05461e9ffd\",\n    \"PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.cs\": \"26019fe6a3e4a2ffb26588a134ddc1e0c535bc49b105869f4aaf0d517ddb931c\",\n    \"PostgreSqlCommandStage.cs\": \"4f57b21e7184419617ef0c0463e4fe68647823c00253cdd62484b7b3b9506e35\",\n    \"PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.cs\": \"326f34ee4cc2fd9695c8b9195a1dcfaf6361afd45d4e8cad29850ec0753a9c70\",\n    \"PostgreSqlContextLease.cs\": \"10e7f584b8bbf373ef2ac31b1cd544f7f9e654a50cabed3f42c67e46b7244e3b\",\n    \"PostgreSqlContextRegistration.cs\": \"280fab4ae346b3f0a8dacd4d61b2690ee6b1379b68a43bf99dc30fbd69b8a2e7\",\n    \"PostgreSqlFailureInfo.cs\": \"12b0a08f39622ca4fbc9cf77e1c54a24c01002e9e1582259f00f2cf90caf7a3c\",\n    \"PostgreSqlOptions.cs\": \"5395b0d391c18d546112ff4de81ad46145cd351d5e91aa2bc1202f50002d5bcb\",\n    \"PostgreSqlPolicy.cs\": \"e4b048bf1cc5e4cba836c00a6a1ac905e1b0562b3352854b5ee87da75b941e3e\",\n    \"PostgreSqlRedactingLogger.cs\": \"d0d2e3275ff46999890b1c3e577ac50d4bb4ffc07f3bc7af77d40f0e5db302e2\",\n    \"PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory.cs\": \"479dc9adac8eb6695846114e3d815ea6351a6fb93a8446d1b21cdc435861c780\",\n    \"PostgreSqlUnitLease.cs\": \"b0232977c646b9120d754af245aa18e4cd509ec2f21eeffb18f88e0c20da8a5b\",\n    \"PostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory.cs\": \"42d730f2021cc13b4ebd2f7b9c3f111c5612e7e34da9170735a4f2cd88d251f8\",\n    \"ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.cs\": \"50bd40a29f743753a4a9ef02c562b99cd6a711deaf9636e349f988816b52d23f\"\n  },\n  \"contracts\": [\n    {\n      \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n      \"owner\": \"Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql\",\n      \"scope\": \"postgresql-policy\",\n      \"complete\": true,\n      \"sources\": {\n        \"ContextLeaseState.cs\": \"0374fda52f16c84224d3b72cb862ef141150f6ffbb38187398cccab1042752c6\",\n        \"FoundationPostgreSqlDbContext.cs\": \"f7607fa8ba617c90d28234ba48b897c774ad84fce9be7ae7d4c53260fa8833ab\",\n        \"FoundationPostgreSqlServiceCollectionExtensions.cs\": \"6e8c7c5d76b1b35522542fdeb9db50411e6308062d01f6ed0fb69a9d59f6a02b\",\n        \"IPostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory.cs\": \"6280f1fc36cafe2c3e5f64de049f0f7494a10e4c80e89dbc422f1775ac8c0b3b\",\n        \"OwnedPostgreSqlDbContextFactory.cs\": \"9472b0df3f4b7fe9ae5f586a116f8f22f22d49cdc591cb7283041d05461e9ffd\",\n        \"PostgreSqlCommandInterceptor.cs\": \"26019fe6a3e4a2ffb26588a134ddc1e0c535bc49b105869f4aaf0d517ddb931c\",\n        \"PostgreSqlCommandStage.cs\": \"4f57b21e7184419617ef0c0463e4fe68647823c00253cdd62484b7b3b9506e35\",\n        \"PostgreSqlConnectionInterceptor.cs\": \"326f34ee4cc2fd9695c8b9195a1dcfaf6361afd45d4e8cad29850ec0753a9c70\",\n        \"PostgreSqlContextLease.cs\": \"10e7f584b8bbf373ef2ac31b1cd544f7f9e654a50cabed3f42c67e46b7244e3b\",\n        \"PostgreSqlContextRegistration.cs\": \"280fab4ae346b3f0a8dacd4d61b2690ee6b1379b68a43bf99dc30fbd69b8a2e7\",\n        \"PostgreSqlFailureInfo.cs\": \"12b0a08f39622ca4fbc9cf77e1c54a24c01002e9e1582259f00f2cf90caf7a3c\",\n        \"PostgreSqlOptions.cs\": \"5395b0d391c18d546112ff4de81ad46145cd351d5e91aa2bc1202f50002d5bcb\",\n        \"PostgreSqlPolicy.cs\": \"e4b048bf1cc5e4cba836c00a6a1ac905e1b0562b3352854b5ee87da75b941e3e\",\n        \"PostgreSqlRedactingLogger.cs\": \"d0d2e3275ff46999890b1c3e577ac50d4bb4ffc07f3bc7af77d40f0e5db302e2\",\n        \"PostgreSqlRedactingLoggerFactory.cs\": \"479dc9adac8eb6695846114e3d815ea6351a6fb93a8446d1b21cdc435861c780\",\n        \"PostgreSqlUnitLease.cs\": \"b0232977c646b9120d754af245aa18e4cd509ec2f21eeffb18f88e0c20da8a5b\",\n        \"PostgreSqlUnitLeaseFactory.cs\": \"42d730f2021cc13b4ebd2f7b9c3f111c5612e7e34da9170735a4f2cd88d251f8\",\n        \"ShellPostgreSqlDataSource.cs\": \"50bd40a29f743753a4a9ef02c562b99cd6a711deaf9636e349f988816b52d23f\"\n      },\n      \"settings\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName}:ConnectionString\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"secret\": true,\n          \"constraints\": {},\n          \"binding\": \"Shell configuration binds Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName} to PostgreSqlOptions; native owner validation admits the resulting values.\",\n          \"precedence\": [\n            \"typed source initializer\",\n            \"ordered shell configuration providers\",\n            \"code configuration registered after binding\"\n          ],\n          \"reload\": \"restart\",\n          \"description\": \"Supported ConnectionString value owned by PostgreSqlOptions.\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName}:OperationTimeout\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"secret\": false,\n          \"constraints\": {\n            \"format\": \"timespan\",\n            \"exclusiveMinimumMilliseconds\": 0,\n            \"maximumMilliseconds\": 2147483647\n          },\n          \"binding\": \"Shell configuration binds Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName} to PostgreSqlOptions; native owner validation admits the resulting values.\",\n          \"precedence\": [\n            \"typed source initializer\",\n            \"ordered shell configuration providers\",\n            \"code configuration registered after binding\"\n          ],\n          \"reload\": \"restart\",\n          \"description\": \"Supported OperationTimeout value owned by PostgreSqlOptions.\",\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"default\": \"00:00:10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName}:ConnectionTimeout\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"secret\": false,\n          \"constraints\": {\n            \"format\": \"timespan\",\n            \"exclusiveMinimumMilliseconds\": 0,\n            \"maximumMilliseconds\": 1024000\n          },\n          \"binding\": \"Shell configuration binds Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName} to PostgreSqlOptions; native owner validation admits the resulting values.\",\n          \"precedence\": [\n            \"typed source initializer\",\n            \"ordered shell configuration providers\",\n            \"code configuration registered after binding\"\n          ],\n          \"reload\": \"restart\",\n          \"description\": \"Supported ConnectionTimeout value owned by PostgreSqlOptions.\",\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"default\": \"00:00:02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName}:CommandTimeout\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"secret\": false,\n          \"constraints\": {\n            \"format\": \"timespan\",\n            \"exclusiveMinimumMilliseconds\": 0,\n            \"maximumMilliseconds\": 2147483647\n          },\n          \"binding\": \"Shell configuration binds Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName} to PostgreSqlOptions; native owner validation admits the resulting values.\",\n          \"precedence\": [\n            \"typed source initializer\",\n            \"ordered shell configuration providers\",\n            \"code configuration registered after binding\"\n          ],\n          \"reload\": \"restart\",\n          \"description\": \"Supported CommandTimeout value owned by PostgreSqlOptions.\",\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"default\": \"00:00:05\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName}:LockTimeout\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"secret\": false,\n          \"constraints\": {\n            \"format\": \"timespan\",\n            \"exclusiveMinimumMilliseconds\": 0,\n            \"maximumMilliseconds\": 2147483647\n          },\n          \"binding\": \"Shell configuration binds Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName} to PostgreSqlOptions; native owner validation admits the resulting values.\",\n          \"precedence\": [\n            \"typed source initializer\",\n            \"ordered shell configuration providers\",\n            \"code configuration registered after binding\"\n          ],\n          \"reload\": \"restart\",\n          \"description\": \"Supported LockTimeout value owned by PostgreSqlOptions.\",\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"default\": \"00:00:01\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName}:CancellationTimeout\",\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"secret\": false,\n          \"constraints\": {\n            \"format\": \"timespan\",\n            \"exclusiveMinimumMilliseconds\": 0,\n            \"maximumMilliseconds\": 2147483647\n          },\n          \"binding\": \"Shell configuration binds Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies:{policyName} to PostgreSqlOptions; native owner validation admits the resulting values.\",\n          \"precedence\": [\n            \"typed source initializer\",\n            \"ordered shell configuration providers\",\n            \"code configuration registered after binding\"\n          ],\n          \"reload\": \"restart\",\n          \"description\": \"Supported CancellationTimeout value owned by PostgreSqlOptions.\",\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"default\": \"00:00:02\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"semanticConstraints\": [\n        \"Each duration must be positive and at most Int32.MaxValue milliseconds; connection/command must fit operation and lock must fit command.\",\n        \"ConnectionTimeout is additionally at most1024000 milliseconds: native Npgsql Timeout is the positive duration rounded up to whole seconds and must not exceed1024 seconds. CommandTimeout is likewise rounded up to at least one whole second; CancellationTimeout rounds up to whole milliseconds. These fallbacks do not replace the independently enforced stage deadlines.\",\n        \"ConnectionString is secret, required and parsed by the native NpgsqlConnectionStringBuilder. Native policy overrides connection/command/cancellation timeout fallbacks and always enables reset-on-close.\",\n        \"PolicyName is application-owned; stable datasource/context-unit ownership is established by explicit AddFoundationPostgreSql registration. No metadata export creates a datasource or connects.\",\n        \"Binding occurs at shell composition; each provider generation owns its validated immutable snapshot and existing work drains before disposal.\"\n      ],\n      \"appliesTo\": {\n        \"kind\": \"shell\",\n        \"features\": [],\n        \"configuration\": [\n          \"Foundation:PostgreSql:Policies\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"typeName\": \"Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.PostgreSqlOptions\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"assembly\": {\n    \"name\": \"Orbyss.Foundation.PostgreSql.dll\",\n    \"sha256\": \"fb408e32bd05bad3477c7425157bd050bb905994070ed1b796d50f251eda0f7d\"\n  },\n  \"imports\": []\n}\n"
  }
